WEBVTT

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.200
This is a story about love.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.290
The princess of a certain country fell in love.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.410
The person she fell in love
with was the castle cook.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.120
Theirs was a love between
people of different social classes.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.120
This is off topic, but why
do we say " <i>fall</i> in love"?

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.080
Is it because one falls into it unexpectedly
and suddenly, like a pitfall trap?

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.040
Not that I would know.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.740
The two of them nurtured their love secretly,

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.240
and in time, the princess became pregnant.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.370
Yes, it was the fruit of
their love, so to speak.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.990
The Princess Without Subjects

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.290
This place is in ruins...

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.740
I wonder if there was a war or something.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.490
I didn't hear anything about that, though.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:08.160
There isn't a single person here...

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.990
Still, this is a problem...

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.160
Even if I head to another town now,

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.370
I probably won't get there
until the middle of the night...

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.830
I'll freeze...

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:35.620
This is the only place that
looks like it's still standing...

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.580
It looks like no one's home.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.870
I am very reluctant to do this,

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.620
but I have to do what I have to do.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.540
Please excuse the intrusion.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.740
Who are you?

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.120
I feel alive again.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.370
It was cold outside, wasn't it?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.410
Yes.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:21.200
At any rate, I didn't think anyone lived here.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:24.620
I didn't think anyone would come here, either.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.830
Where did you come from?

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.830
From a faraway, distant land.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:32.620
I'm a traveler.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.580
May I ask your name?

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.160
I'm Elaina.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.910
My name is Mirarosé.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.330
Nice to meet you.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:48.490
Mirarosé, what happened to this town?

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.450
I don't know...

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.990
You don't?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:58.330
I don't know what happened
to this town, or why I'm here.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.490
When I woke up, I found myself in
this country that was already in ruins.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.120
Do you have amnesia?

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:08.290
Most likely.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.450
But you remember your name?

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.660
"You who are reading this
are the princess, Mirarosé."

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.790
You're a princess?

00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:31.620
You're living in a room like this in the castle,

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.990
so I guess it makes sense.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.830
Oh, okay.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:41.160
"Why are you here? Why is the country in ruins?

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.240
Why have you lost your memory?

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:45.950
I will explain a little.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.160
If you do not want to die, then read this."

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.580
Whoever wrote this seems pretty self-important.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.410
It looks like the sun has set.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:54.870
Right...

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.450
"By the way, is it night where you are?

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.910
If so, then I'd like you
to look out the window."

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.990
Out the window?

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:27.910
What is that?

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.290
Continue reading.

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:33.870
"That monster is the demon
that destroyed the country

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:36.080
and the cause of your amnesia.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.910
The monster's name is Javalier."

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:43.290
Is that... Javalier?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:46.450
The next part of the letter says,

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:51.200
"Awakening as the sun sets,
destroying the country until the sunrise.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:55.950
Javalier's goal is to annihilate
everyone in this country.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:59.080
It is going wild looking for the last person--

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.700
in other words, you."

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.490
Javalier is trying to kill me.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:11.580
Then, why don't you leave this
country and go somewhere else?

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:13.370
"This castle is safe.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.240
Javalier cannot enter this castle."

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:17.200
Why...?

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.330
Who knows?

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.080
Besides--

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.200
"Javalier is after you, she who has
become a princess without subjects.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:29.240
If you leave this country,
then Javalier will chase you," it says.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.790
And then finally, it says,
"I'd like to ask you a favor.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.740
I want you to kill Javalier.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:39.160
As a witch, you should have enough
power to easily defeat Javalier.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.450
Please, for our sake, in order for you to live,

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:45.580
and for the sake of those
unfortunate enough to be killed."

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.040
That's how it is.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.660
Huh.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:54.410
So you're a witch, Mirarosé?

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.290
So you're a witch, too, Elaina?

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:01.410
That should've been obvious by my appearance.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.080
I have my brooch on, too.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:05.040
I'm just kidding.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:11.450
But that letter leaves a lot of questions.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.910
Why did Javalier appear?

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:17.910
Why were you the only one
to survive and lose your memory?

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.620
It doesn't say anything about that.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.120
You're right.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:26.240
But I'm the princess, and this country
was destroyed by that monster.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:29.080
So, I have a duty to defeat that.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.790
Don't you agree?

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.990
How many days have you seen that monster?

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:39.290
It's the seventh day.

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:40.830
Have you ever fought it?

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.660
Not yet.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.990
But, I will fight it tomorrow night.

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:46.950
Do you have any chance of winning?

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:48.870
Of course I do.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:51.700
You seem very confident.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.830
It's been one week since I woke up,

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:57.370
and I finally remembered how to use magic.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:10:03.450
It's possible that before I lost
my memory, I was pretty good.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.790
Moreover, my magic has been recharged.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.740
Do your best.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.200
I will be cheering you on from a safe distance.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.700
Oh my, you won't help me?

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.040
Will I gain anything by helping you?

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:22.490
I don't dislike your honesty.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:24.330
Thanks.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:32.620
And so, Mirarosé let me use
a room once used by a castle servant.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.740
Now...

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.540
It's so fluffy and warm!

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:46.620
Thank you, Mirarosé!

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.040
Something smells good...

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.490
Good morning.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:27.160
Morning. These just finished baking.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.290
Where'd they come from?

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.330
I baked them.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.790
You can bake?

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.040
I can.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:34.910
Even though you're a princess.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:39.040
I don't know why, but my
body just seems to remember.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.490
It's mysterious.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:43.540
Anyway, let's eat while they're still warm.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:48.830
Let's eat!

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:55.660
It's good.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:57.330
I'm glad.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:03.330
Will you listen to me talk
while we eat? About tonight.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.910
You'll be fighting Javalier, right?

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:08.700
I'd like you to help me prepare.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:12.160
You let me spend the night
and even made breakfast.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.040
I can at least help with your preparations.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.080
Then, will you help me fight Javalier?

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:19.540
Sorry, but no.

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.120
Right.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:25.200
Besides, if this place is safe,
like the letter says,

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:28.370
then don't you have the choice of not fighting?

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:32.830
Well, I suppose the letter's
credibility is also questionable, though.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:37.740
The resentment the writer of
that letter felt for Javalier is real.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:40.830
Why do you think that?

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:42.580
I can feel it.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:45.790
"I hate Javalier so much. I want to kill it."

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:47.950
I can feel that hatred.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:51.790
And for some reason, I feel the same way.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:18.240
Well?

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:20.200
Do you think you'll finish by nightfall?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:23.830
Wh-What does "finish" mean in this case?

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:27.660
Let's see. I think you're maybe halfway done?

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.290
I might die first...

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:33.950
Mirarosé's plan is to trick
Javalier into falling into the hole

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:37.740
and then attack with magic
after it is unable to move.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:38.830
I see.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:43.040
Even if just prevents a counterattack,
it could be very effective.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:46.620
The flaw in this plan is that
the preparations are a huge pain.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:51.040
This is nothing! I'm the Ashen Witch!

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:52.790
This is a trifle!

00:13:58.040 --> 00:13:59.450
Thank you for your efforts.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:01.790
It's almost time.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:03.700
Let us meet again later.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.830
I'll treat you to a delicious dinner.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.240
No, thank you.

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:12.950
It will be a lot of work for you
to cook after finishing a big job,

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.490
I will cook.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:17.830
So please don't die.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:21.160
Don't worry. I won't die.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:31.290
Now, go on.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.950
Until later.

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:02.200
I ended up coming.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.870
It's strange.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:06.450
Even though I only met her yesterday,

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:10.370
I couldn't help but feel
like I wanted her to live.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:15.160
So I will fight with her, too.
Without putting my life in danger.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:26.580
Come now, this way!

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:59.040
Come here, Javalier!

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:08.370
It's here.

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:49.120
She did it!

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:23.490
She's strong.

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:26.200
Maybe I won't need to do anything...

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.580
Mirarosé!

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:42.870
So that's how it was.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:09.120
That's amazing...

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:24.290
Well? Do you understand my despair now?

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:32.790
Goodbye...

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:35.200
...Father.

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:50.330
I remember now.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.660
I got my memories back!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.330
All of them!

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:21.080
She told her father, the king, about how
she had become pregnant with the cook's child.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.080
This is what the king said:

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.490
"He will be executed."

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:31.080
The king would not allow their
love that crossed class and rank.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:33.580
The cook underwent cruel torture,

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:37.080
and was burned to death in front of her eyes.

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:41.620
And the child, too...

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:44.870
I swore

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:47.290
that I would kill everything.

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:51.830
First, in order to make
this castle a safe place,

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:54.830
I put up a barrier that only let mages in.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:59.200
That's why Javalier
couldn't get into the castle?

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:05.290
And then, I left myself a letter,

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:08.160
and cursed my father,
turning him into a monster.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.490
In exchange, I lost my memories.

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:16.870
Your father, Javalier, destroyed
the country and its people...

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:20.540
Yes, he ate them himself.

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:24.910
On top of that, he did it while
still aware that he was the king.

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:29.990
That monster ate the subjects
whether the king wished to or not.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:32.490
That should have made
him understand how it felt...

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:37.080
...to have the things dear to
you snatched away from you...

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.620
To understand that despair...

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.490
Okay, the bread's done.

00:21:56.490 --> 00:21:58.290
It's time to eat.

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:00.790
Now, let's eat.

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:10.160
How is it? Is it good?

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:13.540
Really? I'm glad.

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:17.620
It can't compare to the bread you bake, though.

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:18.910
Do you want to eat more?

00:22:18.910 --> 00:22:23.120
Oh, look, you've got jam on your cheek.

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:32.580
In this way, the curtain
fell on the "love story"

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:35.830
that all went according to her plan.

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:40.950
She became the princess
without subjects by her own hand...
